WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.079
Zann's heart pounded with terror. What was Morb doing here?

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.415
He was supposed to be lost in the vortex!

3
00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:14.881
Zann listened as Morb continued to speak. ". . . and I require a few key ingredients before my new masterpiece is complete."

4
00:00:14.882 --> 00:00:18.045
His face twisted into an evil grin.

5
00:00:18.046 --> 00:00:23.632
"Zann?" Perda's voice sounded very loud as she came up behind him. "Did you find the—?"

6
00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:28.785
"Shh," said Zann. He braced himself, waiting for Morb to turn and spot them.

7
00:00:28.786 --> 00:00:31.341
But Morb kept facing the same direction.

8
00:00:31.342 --> 00:00:39.106
Perda had spotted Morb by now too. "Whoa!" she whispered. Then she frowned. "Wait—he's glowing."

9
00:00:39.107 --> 00:00:43.705
Zann stared at the figure. He realized Perda was right.

10
00:00:43.706 --> 00:00:47.779
Morb was glowing from within, just like their cave crawlers.

11
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:52.700
Gliss, Darb, and Zing appeared. "What's going on?" Darb asked.

12
00:00:52.701 --> 00:01:00.013
"It's a hologram, I think." Zann picked up a pebble and tossed it at Morb. It passed right through the villain.

13
00:01:00.014 --> 00:01:09.680
The Morb hologram was still talking. ". . . and then Magica shall be mine!" he cried. "See that you don't fail me."

14
00:01:09.681 --> 00:01:13.908
The image blinked out of sight. A second later it blinked back on.

15
00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:19.087
"Good day," Morb began. "I have need of your services once again . . ."

16
00:01:19.088 --> 00:01:23.973
"It must be a message for someone," Perda guessed. "Maybe Wyssa?"

17
00:01:23.974 --> 00:01:31.393
Zann nodded. "An old message. It's probably been playing over and over again for months."

18
00:01:31.394 --> 00:01:34.147
Gliss shuddered. "Creepy."

19
00:01:34.148 --> 00:01:40.454
"Yeah." Zann took a step closer. Even though he knew the image wasn't real, it made him nervous.

20
00:01:40.455 --> 00:01:46.224
His foot hit something that skittered across the stone floor. "What was that?" Darb asked.

21
00:01:46.225 --> 00:01:51.302
Zann bent to see. "A stone. It looks just like mine!"

22
00:01:51.303 --> 00:01:55.221
"Look." Gliss pointed. "There are lots more!"

23
00:01:55.222 --> 00:02:00.744
The glow of the crawlers showed dozens of identical stones scattered across the chamber floor.

24
00:02:00.745 --> 00:02:05.212
Then Zann noticed something glowing and vibrating in the wall nearby.

25
00:02:05.213 --> 00:02:08.306
"Hey, there's one stuck in the wall."

26
00:02:08.307 --> 00:02:11.309
He touched the stone, which felt warm.

27
00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:16.360
When he tugged on it, it popped out. The hologram instantly vanished.

28
00:02:16.361 --> 00:02:20.681
"Oh!" Perda said. "The stone must contain the message!"

29
00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:26.044
Gliss' eyes widened. "Maybe that's why we landed here," she said.

30
00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:31.402
"Zann's stone might have led us to this spot when the relic zapped us away."

31
00:02:31.403 --> 00:02:37.278
Zann couldn't speak for a second. What if the stone Wyssa had given him held a message from his parents?

32
00:02:37.279 --> 00:02:39.946
He stuck his hand in his pocket and gasped.

33
00:02:39.947 --> 00:02:43.705
His stone was so hot it almost burned his hand.

34
00:02:43.706 --> 00:02:49.117
"Let's try plugging mine into that hole," he said, his voice shaking.

35
00:02:49.118 --> 00:02:51.242
He stepped toward the hole in the wall.

36
00:02:51.243 --> 00:02:54.335
But he hesitated when he heard the clatter of footsteps.

37
00:02:54.336 --> 00:02:57.301
A second later Tok burst into the chamber.

38
00:02:57.302 --> 00:03:00.921
"There you are!" the pilot said breathlessly.

39
00:03:00.922 --> 00:03:06.869
"We felt a huge disruption in energy a few minutes ago, and we were worried about you. What happened?"

40
00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:12.660
"Nothing," Darb said quickly. "We just, uh, tripped over a relic."

41
00:03:12.661 --> 00:03:17.193
Zann shot a look at Gliss, who looked guilty. But Tok didn't seem to notice.

42
00:03:17.194 --> 00:03:23.243
"You must be careful," Tok said with a frown. "The Cave is a dangerous place.

43
00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:25.763
Anyway, you kids need to come back with me.

44
00:03:25.764 --> 00:03:29.167
We're planning to seal off this section of the Cave shortly."

45
00:03:29.168 --> 00:03:32.411
"What?" Zann blurted out. "But I need to—"

46
00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:36.569
Tok didn't let him finish. "No arguments," he said briskly.

47
00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:44.411
"Everyone needs to get out of the Cave before the Magic Masters get to work."

48
00:03:44.412 --> 00:03:48.925
"What do we do now?" Perda wondered, staring at the cave entrance.

49
00:03:48.926 --> 00:03:53.497
Zann didn't answer. He was still angry that Tok had dragged the kids outside.

50
00:03:53.498 --> 00:03:57.671
It wasn't fair! What if that stone held a message from Zann's parents?

51
00:03:57.672 --> 00:04:00.869
"We have to get back in there," he muttered.

52
00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:05.502
Darb glanced over. "How? Tok's guarding the entrance."

53
00:04:05.503 --> 00:04:09.051
Zann spotted Teplo nearby. "I'll be right back."

54
00:04:09.052 --> 00:04:13.556
He hurried over to the Magic Master, checking to be sure that Boz wasn't around.

55
00:04:13.557 --> 00:04:16.666
When Zann described what had happened, Teplo looked guilty.

56
00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:22.128
"You're right, Zann," Teplo said. "It's a message stone. I recognized it right away."

57
00:04:22.129 --> 00:04:26.099
"Why didn't Boz let you tell me that?" Zann asked.

58
00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:30.338
Teplo hesitated and then said, "He's trying to protect you.

59
00:04:30.339 --> 00:04:35.104
Besides, I doubt that stone has anything to do with you or your parents."

60
00:04:35.105 --> 00:04:36.692
"But Wyssa said—"

61
00:04:36.693 --> 00:04:41.888
"You can't trust anything that otherworldly old woman says," Teplo said.

62
00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:46.848
Before Zann could respond, Boz let out a shout and appeared near the cave entrance.

63
00:04:46.849 --> 00:04:51.576
"Oh dear, he doesn't look happy," Teplo muttered, hurrying off.

64
00:04:51.577 --> 00:04:54.062
Zann saw little choice but to follow.

65
00:04:54.063 --> 00:04:59.627
"What's going on?" he asked his friends, who were at the edge of the group gathering around Boz.

66
00:04:59.628 --> 00:05:05.238
"I'm not sure," Gliss whispered. "It sounds like some of the relics are missing."

67
00:05:05.239 --> 00:05:08.473
"Are you sure about this, Boz?" someone called out.

68
00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:12.223
"It's possible that Morb stole some relics that we don't know about."

69
00:05:12.224 --> 00:05:17.022
Boz's nose quivered with dismay. "Yes, that's possible.

70
00:05:17.023 --> 00:05:21.105
But I saw the Mask of Zanta myself an hour ago.

71
00:05:21.106 --> 00:05:24.981
When I went back a few minutes ago, it was gone!"

72
00:05:24.982 --> 00:05:29.505
"The Dragontamer's Charm is missing too," said Uncle Gar.

73
00:05:29.506 --> 00:05:36.219
"I cataloged it earlier. Some minor relics from the same cavern have disappeared as well."

74
00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:40.898
"We'll have to postpone the Sealing spell," Teplo said with a frown.

75
00:05:40.899 --> 00:05:46.586
"We need to get everyone else back here and make sure the relics weren't moved by one of us."

76
00:05:46.587 --> 00:05:50.358
"I'll get Venna," Tok said. "I think she's in the airship."

77
00:05:50.359 --> 00:05:57.810
Zann backed away. Zing followed, though Zann's friends were watching the adults and didn't notice his and Zing's departure.

78
00:05:57.811 --> 00:06:02.790
"Good," thought Zann. He didn't want to get his friends in trouble for what he was about to do.

79
00:06:02.791 --> 00:06:07.060
This could be his only chance to play the message on his stone.

80
00:06:07.061 --> 00:06:13.646
"Quiet, Zing," he whispered. "We're going back in."

